From: codeandsolder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: use logical TCL indices for AHB TX IRQs

The TX group masks index logical TCL rings, as used by the NAPI
completion handler and MSI group calculation. The AHB IRQ setup
instead checks the mapped physical WBM release ring number. On
IPQ5332, logical TCL ring 3 maps to WBM release ring 4, so its
completion IRQ is never registered.

Use the logical index consistently, and iterate only the configured
TX rings rather than the maximum-sized mapping array. Keep the
physical WBM mapping for SRNG configuration.

On Wave 7, ring 3 had 25 enqueues and zero completions while rings
0-2 were balanced, causing repeated TX flush timeouts.

Signed-off-by: codeandsolder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c
@@ -510,9 +510,8 @@ static int ath12k_ahb_config_ext_irq(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 		netif_napi_add(irq_grp->napi_ndev, &irq_grp->napi,
 			       ath12k_ahb_ext_grp_napi_poll);
 
-		for (j = 0; j < DP_TCL_NUM_RING_MAX; j++) {
-			if (ring_mask->tx[i] &
-			    BIT(ab->hal.tcl_to_wbm_rbm_map[j].wbm_ring_num) &&
+		for (j = 0; j < ab->hw_params->max_tx_ring; j++) {
+			if (ring_mask->tx[i] & BIT(j) &&
 			    num_irq < ATH12K_EXT_IRQ_NUM_MAX) {
 				irq_grp->irqs[num_irq++] =
 					wbm2host_tx_completions_ring1 - j;
